Motorola's M68060 Software Package (060/) and M68040 Floating Point Software Package (040/), used by ZINE's CPU
support packages (user/zine/zsp060.S, zsp040.S; docs/d29-zine.md 16.14).

Both are Motorola's, under the licence in 060/README and 040/README (copyright Motorola Inc. 1993, 1994: use,
modification and distribution allowed so long as the notice is kept unchanged and modified versions are identified as
such). That licence asks nothing the GPL-2.0 does not allow; the Linux kernel (GPL-2.0) carries the same files.

Where they come from: the Linux kernel 7.3 tree, arch/m68k/ifpsp060 and arch/m68k/fpsp040.
- 060/: fpsp.sa and isp.sa (Motorola's released hex images, the form the package is supported in), their
  documentation (fpsp.doc, isp.doc, CHANGES, README) and Motorola's source (src/fpsp.S, src/isp.S, src/README-SRC:
  documentation only, it does not build with the GNU assembler). Not changed.
- 040/: the package's source in the GNU assembler's syntax, as the Linux kernel converted it from Motorola's (that
  conversion is a modified version in the licence's sense); the Linux kernel's skeleton.S (its call-outs into Linux)
  is left out, ZINE's own call-outs (user/zine/zsp040.S) take its place. Not changed further.
